{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789406366,"nonce":"Oju2IhXEVmG+H5mFmDE0y46zTvU=","title":"Isolates: a VM per thread with channels, values crossing by copy","message":"The first shape of 6b20a51: every core for a program that partitions\nits work, without touching the single-thread path. One VM per OS\nthread, each with its own heap and scheduler world; a value crosses by\ncopy in a thread-neutral form (null, Bool, Num, String, and List/Map\nof those; anything else is a runtime error naming the class); a\nchannel is a shared queue whose receive parks the caller on its world\nand whose send wakes it through the scheduler's wait registry, so a\ntask can block on a channel while its world keeps running.\n\nSurface, built-in module `isolate` / class `IsolateCore` (handles are\nnumbers; a hatch package wraps them):\n- spawn(module, arg) -\u003e id: a thread runs `import \"module\"` on a fresh\n  VM with `arg` copied in; arg -\u003e that value; isDone(id); error(id) -\u003e\n  String|null (an abort or a module that will not load); join(id, ms)\n  -\u003e Bool; cpus.\n- channel() -\u003e id; send(ch, v) -\u003e Bool (false once closed);\n  receive(ch, ms) -\u003e [v] or null (timeout or closed; ms null waits);\n  tryReceive(ch); close(ch); isClosed(ch); pending(ch); drop(ch).\n\nHow a child VM is made: VM.isolate_factory, an `Arc\u003cdyn Fn() -\u003e VM +\nSend + Sync\u003e` the embedder sets and children inherit. wlift sets one\nthat rebuilds its file loader and spec dependencies; hatch run sets\none that installs the `--with` dependencies and *stages* the program's\nown bundle (VM::stage_hatch_modules: modules are registered and run on\nfirst import, so the child runs only the module it was spawned on).\nWithout a factory the child has the parent's execution settings and\nonly built-in modules.\n\nLeft for later:\n- AOT: an AOT VM has no factory, so spawn's import fails and the\n  isolate ends with an error; running a compiled module body on a\n  fresh VM is its own piece.\n- Channel and isolate handles live for the process (drop(ch) frees a\n  channel; isolates are never removed from the registry).\n- Typed arrays and byte buffers do not cross yet; only the plain data\n  kinds do.\n- The plugin dylibs are loaded per VM; a plugin with process globals\n  is on its own across threads.\n- The sender copies eagerly; large lists cost a copy per hop.","files":null}]}